{"id":"5f363231f41efc07","group":"58","path":"58/batch15/58-df-zfc-sigma-one-formula.md","title":"ZFC Sigma One Formula","display":"df-zfc-sigma-one-formula — ZFC Sigma One Formula","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-zfc-sigma-one-formula","aliases":["58-df-zfc-sigma-one-formula"],"display":"df-zfc-sigma-one-formula — ZFC Sigma One Formula","depends_on":["[[../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md]]","[[../batch17/58-df-formula.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-zfc-delta-zero-formula.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-zfc-sigma-one-formula"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-zfc-sigma-one-formula</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-zfc-sigma-one-formula — ZFC Sigma One Formula"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" href=\"?note=a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" title=\"../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md\">../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-formula.md\">../batch17/58-df-formula.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"2678ecfefaa83e32\" href=\"?note=2678ecfefaa83e32\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-zfc-delta-zero-formula.md\">../batch16/58-df-zfc-delta-zero-formula.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma\">\\(\\Sigma\\)</span> (set-coded first-order signature)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi\\in V\">\\(\\varphi\\in V\\)</span> (formula-code candidate)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Var}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Var}_S\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\">\\(\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\)</span> (variable and formula-code sets, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-formula.md\">../batch17/58-df-formula.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{DeltaZeroFormula}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{DeltaZeroFormula}_S\\)</span> (bounded-formula predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"2678ecfefaa83e32\" href=\"?note=2678ecfefaa83e32\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-zfc-delta-zero-formula\">../batch16/58-df-zfc-delta-zero-formula</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\)</span> (set-coded function predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SigmaOneFormula}_S\\subseteq V^2\">\\(\\mathrm{SigmaOneFormula}_S\\subseteq V^2\\)</span> (predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}sigma\\text{-}one\\text{-}formula}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{SigmaOneFormula}_S(\\varphi,\\Sigma)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\leftrightarrow\n\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\land\n\\exists n\\in\\omega\\;\\exists x\\;\\exists\\theta\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Function}(x,n,\\mathrm{Var}_S)\n\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\theta,n+1,\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma))\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\mathrm{DeltaZeroFormula}_S(\\theta(0),\\Sigma)\n\\land\\theta(n)=\\varphi\n\\land\\forall i\\in n\\;\\bigl(\\theta(i+1)=\\neg\\forall x(i)\\,\\neg\\theta(i)\\bigr)\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}sigma\\text{-}one\\text{-}formula}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{SigmaOneFormula}_S(\\varphi,\\Sigma)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\leftrightarrow\n\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\land\n\\exists n\\in\\omega\\;\\exists x\\;\\exists\\theta\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Function}(x,n,\\mathrm{Var}_S)\n\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\theta,n+1,\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma))\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\mathrm{DeltaZeroFormula}_S(\\theta(0),\\Sigma)\n\\land\\theta(n)=\\varphi\n\\land\\forall i\\in n\\;\\bigl(\\theta(i+1)=\\neg\\forall x(i)\\,\\neg\\theta(i)\\bigr)\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Existential quantification is expanded using the primitive constructors <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\neg\">\\(\\neg\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\forall\">\\(\\forall\\)</span> from the formula-code algebra: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\exists x\\,\\chi\">\\(\\exists x\\,\\chi\\)</span> is coded as <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\neg\\forall x\\,\\neg\\chi\">\\(\\neg\\forall x\\,\\neg\\chi\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>The witness sequence <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\theta\">\\(\\theta\\)</span> makes the finite existential prefix a checkable syntactic construction; the case <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n=0\">\\(n=0\\)</span> includes every bounded formula.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md","status":"resolved","id":"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch17/